  "intro": [
    {
      "title": "Yesterday: your first past tense",
      "title_pl": "Wczoraj: pierwszy czas przeszły",
      "body": "The past of być (to be) fits in one small table — and it does something English can't: the ending tells you who was there, and whether they are male or female.\n\nAll seven forms are built on był-: the verb stem plus -ł-. On a verb, that -ł- before the ending is the past-tense signature — later you'll meet it on every verb (miałem, pracowałem). Only on verbs, though: in words like ładny or szkoła the ł is just a letter.",
      "body_pl": "Czas przeszły być: -ł- w czasowniku = przeszłość, końcówka = osoba.",
      "table": {
        "headers": [
          "Form",
          "Meaning",
          "Used by / for"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "byłem",
            "I was",
            "man speaking (m)"
          ],
          [
            "byłam",
            "I was",
            "woman speaking (f)"
          ],
          [
            "byłeś",
            "you were",
            "to a man (m)"
          ],
          [
            "byłaś",
            "you were",
            "to a woman (f)"
          ],
          [
            "był",
            "he was",
            "on · tata, pies, film"
          ],
          [
            "była",
            "she was",
            "ona · mama, kawa"
          ],
          [
            "było",
            "it was",
            "ono · dziecko, piwo"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "The pattern under it",
      "title_pl": "Wzór",
      "body": "The stem był- never changes. Men's forms take -em / -eś, women's take -am / -aś — the same -a that marks feminine nouns (mama, kawa).\n\nThis is the payoff of all your gender work: things use their gender too. Kawa była (f). Piwo było (n). Film był (m). The noun's gender picks the verb form — automatically, by the badges you already know.\n\nWe were / they were come later, in their own unit. Singular first.",
      "body_pl": "był- + em/am/eś/aś/–/a/o. Rzeczy też: kawa była, piwo było, film był.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "The coffee was good.",
          "pl": "Kawa była dobra."
        },
        {
          "en": "The beer was good.",
          "pl": "Piwo było dobre."
        },
        {
          "en": "The film was good.",
          "pl": "Film był dobry."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Where were you?",
      "title_pl": "Gdzie byłeś?",
      "body": "Every place you can be in (w domu, w pracy, w szkole...) now works in the past. Add wczoraj (yesterday) and you are telling stories.",
      "body_pl": "Wszystkie miejsca z w + miejscownik działają w przeszłości.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I was at home. (m)",
          "pl": "Byłem w domu."
        },
        {
          "en": "Where were you yesterday? (to a woman)",
          "pl": "Gdzie byłaś wczoraj?"
        },
        {
          "en": "Mum was at work.",
          "pl": "Mama była w pracy."
        },
        {
          "en": "The child was at school.",
          "pl": "Dziecko było w szkole."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
